hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20869","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, al-Hasan narrated to us, from Sa'sa'ah ibn Mu'awiyah, uncle of al-Farazdaq, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he recited to him: So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it. He said: It suffices me; I do not care not to hear other than it."
"20870","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: Sa'sa'ah ibn Mu'awiyah, uncle of al-Farazdaq, narrated to us, he said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I heard him recite this verse, then he mentioned its meaning."
"20871","Affan narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Hasan say: The uncle of al-Farazdaq, Sa'sa'ah, came to Madinah when he heard: Whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it. He said: It suffices me; I do not care not to hear other than this."
